# binaries & profiles
*.test
*.out
*.prof
# ...except under archive/, where `.out` is the convention for an instrument's recorded
# output because `.txt` is reserved for raw benchmark logs (tools/benchci globs those and
# fails on a match that yields no readings). The two conventions collide: following the
# archive convention put the evidence a published report cites inside `*.out` above, and
# `git add -A` then skipped it in silence. archive/addr147's `.out` files are tracked only
# by accident of history -- they were committed under their first, wrong `.txt` names and a
# rename keeps a tracked file tracked. archive/width148's were not, and nothing said so.
!archive/**/*.out
/bin/
# `go build ./tools/...` drops this in the repo root
/shapegen
# spill-audit artifacts (archived per-commit under docs/ssa when wanted)
ssa.html
# gate scratch: build/ssa holds one ssa.html per audited kernel, ~5 MB each.
# Not committed — the gate regenerates it on every run, and a stale copy would be
# worse than none when writing docs/spill-report.md.
/build/
# generated documentation-site pages (scripts/docs-gen.sh, run by `make docs`).
# Two reasons they are not committed, one per generation mechanism: the records
# are symlinks into the repository, so committing them would put a second path to
# DESIGN.md in the tree; numbers.md and methodology.md are extractions, so a
# committed copy could disagree with the file it was extracted from and nothing
# would notice. The tracked artifacts are mkdocs.yml, the hand-written user
# pages, and the generator.
/doc-site/numbers.md
/doc-site/records/design.md
/doc-site/records/methodology.md
/doc-site/records/rulings.md
/doc-site/records/toolchain-notes.md
/doc-site/records/kernel.md
/doc-site/records/changelog.md
/doc-site/records/contributing.md
# bench scratch
bench/results/*.local.*
# machine-local remote execution targets (see .keel-hosts.example, docs/hosts.md)
/.keel-hosts
# machine-local P3 gate target: the throughput regression sentinel. Hostnames are
# infrastructure, not source; absent means "every host", never "skip the check"
# (scripts/gate-p3.sh criterion 5). There is no OpenBLAS reference-host list any
# more — the ruling on issue #23 made the reference same-host on every gate host.
/.keel-sentinel
# tools/shapegen candidate scratch. Under internal/vec because that is where simd
# imports live; dot-prefixed so `go ./...` cannot pick up a crashed sweep's leftovers.
/internal/vec/.shapegen-*
# Python bytecode. The #147 analysis instruments import each other (control147.py and
# sensitivity147.py both `from analyze147 import ...`), so running any of them writes a
# __pycache__ beside the archived evidence -- and `git add -A archive/addr147` tracked one
# before this line existed. Bytecode is a build artifact of a specific interpreter version
# and reproduces nothing.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
